 R←TestSelectors;m;b;pairs;tables;p;t;got;exp
⍝ Orbital-element selectors take the element table as their argument
⍝ and agree with the book's selectors, which read ORB from their caller
 m←## ⋄ b←##.Data ⋄ R←1
 pairs←('SemiMajor' 'SEMIMAJOR')('Period' 'PERIOD')('Eccentricity' 'ECCENTRICITY')
 pairs,←('Inclination' 'INCLINATION')('Ascending' 'ASCENDING')('Periangle' 'PERIANGLE')
 pairs,←('Anomaly' 'ANOMALY')('Secular' 'SECULAR')('EpochDate' 'EPOCHDATE')
 pairs,←('AnomalyDate' 'ANOMALYDATE')('PeriDist' 'PERIDIST')('PeriDate' 'PERIDATE')
 tables←b.planets b.moon b.kohoutek (b.planets[,3;])
 :For p :In pairs
     :For t :In tables
         got←(⊃p)m.{⍎⍺,' ⍵'}t
         exp←t b.{ORB←⍺ ⋄ ⍎⍵}2⊃p
         :If got≢exp
             ⎕←'FAIL: TestSelectors: ',(⊃p),' on ',(⍕⍴t),' table' ⋄ R←0
         :EndIf
     :EndFor
 :EndFor
 :If R
     ⎕←'PASS: TestSelectors (',(⍕≢pairs),' selectors, ',(⍕≢tables),' tables)'
 :EndIf
